diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index d99d101..06a05b7 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+- Limiter state and snapshots carry `reset_at`, the clock time the limiter is full again, in place of the relative `reset_in`.
 - Fixed: a hit costing more than the limit (a bucket's capacity) was told to retry later although it could never succeed, and crashed with IndexError on a sliding window. It now raises the same ValueError as a cost below 1, whose message becomes `cost must be between 1 and {limit}: {cost}`, and spends nothing.
 - `TokenBucket` takes `refill_period` (seconds from empty to full) instead of `refill_per_second`.
 - `Decision.retry_after` (and a snapshot's `retry_after`) is now whole milliseconds, rounded up, instead of float seconds.
diff --git a/docs/reference.md b/docs/reference.md
index 1dfc8f5..acdddc3 100644
--- a/docs/reference.md
+++ b/docs/reference.md
@@ -36,14 +36,14 @@ Returned by `hit()` on a limiter or a Throttle.
 ## Limiter state and snapshots
 
 `state()` on a limiter returns a dict; `Throttle.snapshot()` returns one such
-dict per key, sorted by key, with `key`, `policy` and `retry_after` added.
+dict per key, sorted by key, with `key`, `policy` and `retry_after` added. Its `reset_at` is the clock time at
+which the limiter is full again, or the current time if it already is.
 
 | Fact | Value | Meaning |
 |---|---|---|
 | `state.kind` | `fixed, sliding or bucket` | Which algorithm. |
 | `state.limit` | `int` | Limit, or a bucket's capacity. |
 | `state.remaining` | `int` | Units available now. |
-| `state.reset_in` | `float seconds until full again` | 0 when nothing is spent. |
 | `snapshot.key` | `str` | The key. |
 | `snapshot.policy` | `policy text` | The key's policy, written as `parse_policy` reads it. |
 | `snapshot.retry_after` | `same unit as decision.retry_after` | What a hit of 1 would be told now. |
